{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule","id":1487511,"title":"V5 Oblivion - Stains House Rule","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-07-22T14:59:35-07:00","id":1487511,"title":"V5 Oblivion - Stains House Rule","content":"Hi. I've seen a really big thread about Oblivion criticisms (specially Stains cost), and thought of a House Rule.<br /> <br /> <i>I'd like to know your opinions about it. Would it work? What kind of things would emerge from it?</i><br /> <br /> Here's it: <b>Whenever an Oblivion use would make you gain Hunger, you may instead choose to gain 1 Stain per point of Hunger you chose to avoid.</b><br /> <br /> (Rationale: you may choose to use &quot;the power of darkness&quot; to fuel the Discipline, but in order to do so, you must channel it through yourself and get Stained by it in the process).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T15:32:42-07:00","id":1487514,"title":"","content":"I'd just dump it outright. Oblivion isn't any worse than Dominate or Presence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-22T17:03:16-07:00","id":1487519,"title":"","content":"That's before or after rolling the Hunger dice? This will make a huge difference.<br /> <br /> But then, here's the thing: if you do it before rolling, this is a trap option unless the character is already too hungry, maybe even then, because the long term effects of rolling Hunger are significantly minor in comparison with the long term effects of rolling Remorse. On the other hand, if it is after rolling Hunger, then it is exceedingly good to be able to chose between a guaranteed increase in Hunger vs a Remorse roll that may come out as nothing.<br /> <br /> In both cases you're changing a double cost to a choice of cost, which makes Oblivion from worse to better than other Disciplines. It is a better situation, but not necessarily a good situation.<br /> <br /> More importantly, though: what's your goal with this mechanic? What do you want as an effect i the game? What does that represent and how do you want players and STs to roleplay the characters? Do you think Oblivion makes the characters just more pale? More debased? More crazy? Without a clear goal for the mechanic it is hard to measure if it is a good mechanic to begin with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T09:36:58-07:00","id":1487894,"title":"","content":"Assuming it's after a failed rouse check, i think it's a pretty interesting mechanic. It would make oblivion more powerful, but it would reinforce the theme of the abyss being a corrupting influence.<br /> <br /> As written, Oblivion seems pretty ''meh'' compared to most discipline, which doesn't justify the 20% stain risk on each uses of its powerful (beside the 1st level of course). Your proposed idea instead twist the idea around and give something in return for extra risk. Sure, it makes the discipline more powerful, but the bargain isn't risk free. With humanity being so hard to regain that risking losing a dot to avoid getting hungrier is a though call. <br /> <br /> What i'd probably add is the caveat that convictions cannot reduce stains incurred that way. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T17:24:22-07:00","id":1487953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487894#post1487894\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It would make oblivion more powerful, but it would reinforce the theme of the abyss being a corrupting influence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on what you consider as being a corrupting influence.<br /> <br /> It would reinforce the idea that using Oblivion takes a toll on your soul, resulting in much the same consequences as killing someone. And that's pretty neat for some concepts and certainly better than the current rule.<br /> <br /> <b>But</b>, with your powers giving you reason to save &quot;Stain Slots&quot; so you can use them without a Hunger cost, that can still mean that such characters will actually avoid incurring Stains even more than usual now that they are such a nice resource to spend with Disciplines. So you may end up with goody-two-shoes Necromancers and Shadow Manipulators that chose the side of Good\u2122 because it has literal and very concrete benefits in power. And with Hunger going up slower because they can avoid it, there's even less pressure for them to lose control and risk Stains outside using their powers.<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily a bad concept, plenty of Necromancers outside the Giovanni used to be like that, but it may be more unbalanced than it seems at first (it would have to be tested) and may not be what you're aiming at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T19:17:54-07:00","id":1487965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487953#post1487953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends on what you consider as being a corrupting influence.<br /> <br /> It would reinforce the idea that using Oblivion takes a toll on your soul, resulting in much the same consequences as killing someone. And that's pretty neat for some concepts and certainly better than the current rule.<br /> <br /> <b>But</b>, with your powers giving you reason to save &quot;Stain Slots&quot; so you can use them without a Hunger cost, that can still mean that such characters will actually avoid incurring Stains even more than usual now that they are such a nice resource to spend with Disciplines. So you may end up with goody-two-shoes Necromancers and Shadow Manipulators that chose the side of Good\u2122 because it has literal and very concrete benefits in power. And with Hunger going up slower because they can avoid it, there's even less pressure for them to lose control and risk Stains outside using their powers.<br /> <br /> This isn't necessarily a bad concept, plenty of Necromancers outside the Giovanni used to be like that, but it may be more unbalanced than it seems at first (it would have to be tested) and may not be what you're aiming at.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's an interesting side-effect that I wouldn't want. Discovering these is precisely the reason I made this thread. :-] Thank you!<br /> <br /> So, taking this in consideration, I'd change the rule for something closer than the actual one: <b>rolling 10 in a Rouse Check = 1 Stain</b>. That's it. It retains the &quot;I'm a little afraid of getting a Stain&quot;, but since it's only in a 10, it necessarily means that, at least, your Hunger won't rise, and it's a 10% chance. You take away the choice/resource management game feel, and also get rid of the Good\u2122 Necromancer problem. :-]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-25T22:02:36-07:00","id":1487977,"title":"","content":"I would personally go in the opposite direction. Instead of Oblivion giving Stains, having Oblivion <i>avoiding</i> them. It could be that when you use it on an action that would incur a Stain, you take 1 less Stain if you succeed in the Rouse Check.<br /> <br /> Why? Because this has the opposite effect, it encourages players to take risks. Such a character can <b>act</b> more debased precisely because they have <u>less</u> risk of facing the consequences. But then, are prone to go further precisely because of the extra protection, and end up biting some of it anyway.<br /> <br /> Both options make for tropes that do exist in the setting already: historically Cappadocians, Samedi, Lamia and even the Nagaraja had been among the less predatory vampires in their actions and even in their <b>Necromancy</b> Paths, but the more physically marred by their link to the Dark Umbra (a lot of death-related, self-image body horror, gore or both). The Giovanni, though, epitomize <b>Necromancy</b> as a degenerate practice in the hands of degenerate people, that yet are too good at hiding their monstrous tendencies.<br /> <br /> Abyss Mysticism and Obtenebration share similar considerations, but with other considerations entirely. While I think the rules using Stains were meant mainly with the Lasombra in mind, I actually think it fits them poorly. They have a more Lovecraftian feel that I don't think this mechanic serves all that well, specially the Mystics, although it wouldn't be all that of a problem for usual Obtenebration.<br /> <br /> My own take would be to change the effect from a general rule to specific rules tied to specific powers, and/or have Loresheets that cover this and take the extra mechanic out of the Discipline itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T02:33:50-07:00","id":1487993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487965#post1487965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> That's an interesting side-effect that I wouldn't want. Discovering these is precisely the reason I made this thread. :-] Thank you!<br /> <br /> So, taking this in consideration, I'd change the rule for something closer than the actual one: <b>rolling 10 in a Rouse Check = 1 Stain</b>. That's it. It retains the &amp;quot;I'm a little afraid of getting a Stain&amp;quot;, but since it's only in a 10, it necessarily means that, at least, your Hunger won't rise, and it's a 10% chance. You take away the choice/resource management game feel, and also get rid of the Good\u2122 Necromancer problem. :-]</div> </div> </div> </div>I think this could be a neat balance. Though the easiest fix is to still ignore that rule (Oblivion use itself might trigger stains because it's generally a nasty Discipline).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T07:53:36-07:00","id":1488029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487953#post1487953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>But</b>, with your powers giving you reason to save &quot;Stain Slots&quot; so you can use them without a Hunger cost, that can still mean that such characters will actually avoid incurring Stains even more than usual now that they are such a nice resource to spend with Disciplines. So you may end up with goody-two-shoes Necromancers and Shadow Manipulators that chose the side of Good\u2122 because it has literal and very concrete benefits in power. And with Hunger going up slower because they can avoid it, there's even less pressure for them to lose control and risk Stains outside using their powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s a good point, something i hadn\u2019t considered. However i think there\u2019s ways to mitigate the issue and have a bit of both \u2018\u2019world\u2019\u2019.<br /> One one hand, as you said, it could reinforce the idea of necromancers with strict ethical codes to resist the dark pull of the abyss. Which, i think is a pretty cool idea.<br /> On the other hand, with V5 convictions, it\u2019s possible to create some truly horrible characters. Those kind of necromancers/abyss mystics could negate stain with the right convictions.<br /> Lets takes these three convictions for example;<ul><li>The strongs should govern the weak.</li> <li>Kindness is a weakness.</li> <li>Never act in a merciful way..</li> </ul>A character with that set of convictions would probably be fine acting horribly even in a \u2018\u2019humanist\u2019\u2019 chronicle. Of course convictions are always up to the ST approval, but i\u2019m only trying to show that while the mechanics would reinforce a play style, it\u2019s still possible to play the archetypical evil necromancer.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Timecrafter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487965#post1487965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, taking this in consideration, I'd change the rule for something closer than the actual one: <b>rolling 10 in a Rouse Check = 1 Stain</b>. That's it. It retains the &quot;I'm a little afraid of getting a Stain&quot;, but since it's only in a 10, it necessarily means that, at least, your Hunger won't rise, and it's a 10% chance. You take away the choice/resource management game feel, and also get rid of the Good\u2122 Necromancer problem. :-]</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with having stains occurs outside of the character control is that, in my opinion, is twofold;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Oblivion is not powerful enough to justify risking losing humanity over it. Without the stains risk, it\u2019s on part with most other disciplines with the addition that the blood resonance is a little bit more complicated to get.</li> <li>I find that gaining stains outside of the result of your character\u2019s choice is a bit of annoying mechanic. Sure, stains can be incurred through messy bestial critical failures or out of frenzy, which i think are fine as they don\u2019t tend to happen too often and can be mitigated in some way. Beside everyone has to deal with it. With oblivion, it just feels like punishing someone unnecessarily for their choice of power.</li> </ol><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1487977#post1487977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would personally go in the opposite direction. Instead of Oblivion giving Stains, having Oblivion <i>avoiding</i> them. It could be that when you use it on an action that would incur a Stain, you take 1 less Stain if you succeed in the Rouse Check.<br /> <br /> Why? Because this has the opposite effect, it encourages players to take risks. Such a character can <b>act</b> more debased precisely because they have <u>less</u> risk of facing the consequences. But then, are prone to go further precisely because of the extra protection, and end up biting some of it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>That\u2019s also an interesting idea, i like it! However there might be a tiny flaw? With most rouse checks happening before you can do anything with the power, how would you deal with the fact that the vampires would know when to act horribly and when to restrain themselves? For example, the way a lasombra would act with its \u2018\u2019arms of Ahriman\u2019\u2019 might change on a failed or succeeded rouse check. Although, that might be a feature instead of a bug<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T08:05:15-07:00","id":1488031,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Algarik</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488029#post1488029\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although, that might be a feature instead of a bug</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. And if it isn't, well, generally you declare your whole action instead of declaring you activate the power and roll Hunger before declaring what you'll do with it in the same turn. But yeah, together it becomes kind of a moot point, it just gives the player the option to hold on the last minute to not incur that Stain if they don't want to, which isn't all that of a problem at first glance.<br /> <br /> Again, playtesting is needed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T09:18:35-07:00","id":1488036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488031#post1488031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. And if it isn't, well, generally you declare your whole action instead of declaring you activate the power and roll Hunger before declaring what you'll do with it in the same turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, in the case of ''Arms of Ahriman, given that you specifically need to spend a turn to summon them, any actions that might incur stains are bound to happen later, but i guess the ST could ask for the intent before the rouse check is made. Some other powers may have a similar issue, but i'm not aware of all oblivion powers at the top of my head. <br /> <br /> It would probably work well for Hecata powers which generally deal with inflciting some horrible disease on living creatures, or include human sacrifice as part of their ritual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488031#post1488031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But yeah, together it becomes kind of a moot point, it just gives the player the option to hold on the last minute to not incur that Stain if they don't want to, which isn't all that of a problem at first glance.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, after all, especially as an ST coming from Requiem 2e, i've always seen humanity as a way to keep the beast at bay rather than morality. There's also something frightening about a monster with high humanity, that low humanity monster can't convey.<br /> <br /> However, requiem aside, if oblivion users can ''choose'' when to act horribly and not based on their rolls, it kinda goes against the theme of risk and corruption. Oblivion would risk becoming a discipline that protects against the beast rather than eroding humanity, which could work in some medium, but would go against what VtM is trying to convey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488031#post1488031\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, playtesting is needed</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. Still, a cool idea. I'll try to let you know if i end up having the chance to test it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T10:25:36-07:00","id":1488047,"title":"","content":"Because it's come up: does anyone actually use the blood resonance rules?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T10:31:03-07:00","id":1488048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488047#post1488047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's come up: does anyone actually use the blood resonance rules?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I very rarely see it come up. Occasionally an ST will say something like the &quot;blood tastes sanquine&quot; or whatever, and that's about it. I think most ST's consider it just pointless extra bookkeeping that gets in the way of whatever story they are trying to tell. I can imagine a story in which it would be important, like a story about the Circulatory System, or a story about where struggling for the juiciest hunting territories. But I haven't seen such a story happen since V5 began.<br /> <br /> Most VTM games are about fancy parties, detective work, and asskicking. Keeping track of blood resonance is just a boring derailment from the perspective of most STs in their fancy party, detective work, asskicking games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-26T11:07:33-07:00","id":1488057,"title":"","content":"I haven't had the chance to play V5 just yet, hopefully my future ST's campaign will be ready soon and i'll get the chance to experience it from a player point of view. I also plan on running a campaign after i'm done with my requiem Tokyo by night current campaign.<br /> <br /> Is is blood resonance that bad on bookeeping? Seing that there's only 4, 5 if you account for the lack of resonance oblivion need. It didn't seem like too much of a hassle to deal with. The resonnance only seems to matter when you wanna improve discipline and when an intense or acute resonance is involved. <br /> <br /> Idk, doesn't seem that bad to deal with and it can even had some plot hook in the form of high value blood dool, or in a field of study for vampire interested in such. <br /> <br /> Anyway, the oblivion ''lack of resonance'' problem is very minor. It's more of a problem in chronicles that includes those, because it seems like a resonance you can't really manipulate in someone and it seems rarer than the other. Which is small, but an extra negative side of an already mediocre discipline.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26771-algarik","name":"Algarik","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26771_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"115"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T06:32:15-07:00","id":1488161,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488048#post1488048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> I very rarely see it come up. Occasionally an ST will say something like the &amp;quot;blood tastes sanquine&amp;quot; or whatever, and that's about it. I think most ST's consider it just pointless extra bookkeeping that gets in the way of whatever story they are trying to tell. I can imagine a story in which it would be important, like a story about the Circulatory System, or a story about where struggling for the juiciest hunting territories. But I haven't seen such a story happen since V5 began.<br /> <br /> Most VTM games are about fancy parties, detective work, and asskicking. Keeping track of blood resonance is just a boring derailment from the perspective of most STs in their fancy party, detective work, asskicking games.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's pretty much my experience too. We mostly play V20, but have tried V5 a few times, and everyone noped out of using the Blood Resonance rules as either too fiddly or too gamey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-27T19:19:03-07:00","id":1488239,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1487511-v5-oblivion-stains-house-rule?p=1488047#post1488047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because it's come up: does anyone actually use the blood resonance rules?</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess only troupes that started playing VtM using V5 will use Blood Resonance extensively. Older players will probably avoid it or only pay lip service, simply due to not being used to taking it in consideration in their pre-V5 games. I'm pre V5 (I'm originally from 2nd edition LOL), but I do intend to use it fully in my games. I'm open to really try V5 as its own product, in its own terms, to actually see what it delivers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1001-timecrafter","name":"Timecrafter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1001_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}